The deposited files media holds, in the stand-in layout the VRE bridge writes: one directory per
project shortcode, holding the Ready token .ready and the generation it names. CPE reads them through
its bytes port (LiveDepositedFiles in areas/access/media/store). The fixture is a test input and, until
access-server's image stops carrying it, the data the image serves; in a deployment with the VRE
bridge, the bridge's output replaces it.

0803/.ready is hand-written and holds the same bytes as areas/access/sync/data/0803/.ready, which
describes its fields: the two tokens hold equal provenance. The files below are in its generation,
0803/20261007T000000Z-00000000/. The generation has no access-rights.json, which the bridge writes
into every generation (no reader reads it yet), and no file-manifest.json, which it writes for a DaTEI
project: the shipped inputs reserve both names, so the gate below forbids them in the fixture.

config.kdl, curation.csv and narrative/ in that generation are a copy of the VRE bridge's shipped
inputs of project 0803 (incunabula), areas/deposit/vre-bridge/inputs/0803/, which are the
authoritative copy: a change is made there and copied here in the same commit, and
`just check-stand-in-fixture` (run by `just check`) fails while the two differ by a byte or a file.
Where each file came from, and how it is edited, is recorded in areas/deposit/vre-bridge/inputs/PROVENANCE.

A change to the remodel {} block of config.kdl changes Incunabula's store, which cpe-server's
Incunabula store pins hold; a narrative file the configuration names and media does not hold leaves
the project not ready. Every row of curation.csv names a resource of sync's 0803 snapshot,
areas/access/sync/data/0803/20261007T000000Z-00000000/snapshot.nq. If a regenerated snapshot drops
one, CPE leaves Incunabula not ready until the row is removed or re-keyed by hand.
